    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `locality` derivation from an owner's city using the fixed table (Sydney\u2192NSW, Melbourne\u2192VIC, Brisbane\u2192QLD, else `UNKNOWN`).\n\nSince `locality` is a derived, read-only response field (like the existing `displayName`, `initials`, and `membershipTier`), the natural home was the response mapping rather than a new OfficeFloor pipeline step:\n\n1. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `locality` property to the `Owner` schema, which regenerates `OwnerDto` with a `locality` field.\n2. **`LocalityLookup.java`** (new) \u2014 a small helper holding the fixed city-to-region table; `regionOf(city)` returns the canonical region or `\"UNKNOWN\"` (also null-safe).\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 imported `LocalityLookup` into the MapStruct `@Mapper` and added a `@Mapping` expression populating `locality` from `owner.getCity()`.\n\nBoth endpoints that serialize an owner (`GET /api/owners/{id}` and `POST /api/owners`) go through `toOwnerDto`, so the field is populated consistently. The two new acceptance tests (`coreDerivesRegionForKnownCity` \u2192 `NSW` for Sydney, and `functionalityUnknownCityIsUnknown` \u2192 `UNKNOWN` for a random city) both pass.",
